#[$in title:["Templates"]]
#[$in description:["Template strings, directives, slots, wrappers, control flow and Markdown in Moth."]]
#[$in head:[language_theme_head]]

#[navbar]
#[sidebar]
init_docs_sidebar()!
#[section, $md:
    # Templates

    Templates form Moth's only string-composition system. Square brackets can
    join short values, format Markdown or HTML and compose larger layouts with
    slots, wrappers and control flow. Template `$` directives remain owned
    here; the accepted general directive family is documented at
    @../directives (Directives).

    Other languages often split this work across concatenation, interpolation
    and a separate template language. Moth keeps one typed `String` result and
    lets the compiler fold it when every input comes from compile time.
]

